<title>USA: Wells Fargo &amp; Co Q3 shr eases.</title>
<headline>Wells Fargo &amp; Co Q3 shr eases.</headline>
<text>
<p>SAN FRANCISCO, Oct 15 (Reuter)</p>
<p>			 Sept 30, 1996		 Sept 30,1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $3.23		    $5.23</p>
<p> Net			    321			261</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    93.7		     47.9</p>
<p>	     Nine MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			 $11.42		   $14.14</p>
<p> Net			    948			726</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    78.8		     49.2</p>
<p>(All data above in millions except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: In Q3 '96, cash EPS $4.52, cash return on average assets was 1.77 pct, cash return on equity was 31.91 pct.</p>
<p>Q3 and nine months 1996 results reflect First Interstate merger beginning April 1.</p>
<p>Net loan loss provision in Q3 1996 was $35 million, net charge-offs in Q3 totalled $171 million or 0.98 pct of average loans.</p>
<p>Net interest income on taxable-equivalent basis was $1,299 million in Q3. Net interest margin for Q3 was 6.15 percent vs 5.9 pct.</p>
